  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Organizing Food Data**\n\nI\'m now focused on structuring the Indian food data into a modular code module, `src/data.ts`. My aim is to cleanly encapsulate dish details, pricing, descriptions, nutritional information, and serving size calculations, ensuring the main page remains organized and maintainable.\n\n\n**Defining Menu Items**\n\nI\'ve started designing the `MenuItem` interface within `src/data.ts`, establishing categories for starters, juices, main courses, and desserts. I\'m focusing on attributes like ID, name, category, type (veg/non-veg), price, unit, and a crucial `factorPerGuest` for quantity calculations. I\'ve also incorporated a `description`, popularity flag, and spiciness level, to add rich representation. The pricing will use Indian Rupees (\342\202\271) for authenticity.\n\n\n**Populating Item Data**\n\nI\'m now populating the menu with concrete examples, focusing on starters. I\'ve added dishes like *Paneer Tikka Shashlik*, *Cocktail Samosas*, and their corresponding details. I\'m assigning spiciness levels from zero to three and including prices in Indian Rupees. I\'m also ensuring the categorization (veg/non-veg) and popularity flags are accurately reflected in the data. I\'m focusing on descriptive visual aids now, to improve user experience.\n\n\n**Adding Beverage Choices**\n\nI\'m now expanding the menu with beverage selections. I\'ve focused on juices and refreshers, incorporating items like *Mango Lassi*, *Shahi Masala Chaas*, and *Nimbu Sharaf*. I\'ve detailed their key attributes: veg/non-veg status, spice level, and price per guest in Indian Rupees, along with short descriptions and popularity. Now, I\'ll move on to populating the main courses.\n\n\n**Incorporating Main Courses**\n\nI\'ve added the main courses and their details. The focus is now on dishes like *Butter Chicken*, *Dal Makhani*, *Peshawari Chole*, *Kashmiri Awadhi Mutton Biryani*, *Banarasi Subz Biryani* and *Assorted Indian Breads*, alongside non-veg/veg status, spice level, price per guest, and popularity. I\'m focusing on ensuring rich, descriptive details that enhance the user experience.\n\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will now create a data file `/src/data.ts` which contains the structured and detailed definitions of our Indian catering menu items, including details like diet type (veg/non-veg), spice levels, prices, recommended calculation factors, and rich traditional descriptions. This avoids cluttering the main component code."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 944312991
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
